# pyenv
#   For a library or app, you might want to share your .python-version.
#   Normally, this should be in the global gitignore unless you have a
#   compelling reason to share it.
#.python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version control.
#   However, in case of collaboration, if used with a virtualenv, the lock file should be tracked.
#   If you are mapping to a virtualenv, ignore virtualenv folders.
#   See: https://pipenv.pypa.io/en/latest/advanced/#pipenv-and-version-control
#Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, poetry.lock is generally recommended to be tracked.
#   https://python-poetry.org/docs/basic-usage/#commit-your-poetrylock-file-to-version-control
#poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pdm.lock is generally recommended to be tracked.
#.pdm.toml
#.pdm-plugins/
#pdm.lock

# pipspec
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, pipspec.lock is generally recommended to be tracked.
#pipspec.lock

# PEP 582; used by e.g. github.com/lincolnloop/pip-shims
__pypackages__/

